-- An exception inside an operand of RAND or ROR, in a trace (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118).
--
-- When an operand of a compound refuses, divides by zero, matches no branch or
-- needs an input that has no value, #EVALTRACE shows where it happened: a line
-- marked with an arrow under the compound, and another at the end. What sits
-- between a compound and an operand is what gives the operand the time and the
-- events; an extra step there moves the first of the two lines, and for the
-- shapes below it would go missing. The value and the exit code are the same
-- either way, so only a trace shows it, and nothing else in the corpus traces
-- a compound whose operand raises.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alice, Bob
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
  pay HAS amount IS A NUMBER
  deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`plain del` MEANS PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 6

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`div leg` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN (6 / 0)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`refuse leg` MEANS REFUSE "not modelled"

GIVEN k IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nonex leg` k MEANS
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN 1 THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN 2 THEN FULFILLED

§ `Gates`
  GIVEN gate IS A BOOLEAN

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`stuck leg` MEANS
    IF gate THEN PARTY Alice MUST pay 1 WITHIN 5 ELSE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`refuse then fulfilled` MEANS `refuse leg` ROR FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`fulfilled then refuse` MEANS FULFILLED ROR `refuse leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`refuse and del` MEANS `refuse leg` RAND `plain del`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`del and refuse` MEANS `plain del` RAND `refuse leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`div then fulfilled` MEANS `div leg` ROR FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nonex then fulfilled` MEANS `nonex leg` 3 ROR FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`stuck then fulfilled` MEANS `stuck leg` ROR FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nested` MEANS (`refuse leg` RAND `plain del`) ROR FULFILLED

#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `refuse then fulfilled` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `fulfilled then refuse` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `refuse and del` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `del and refuse` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `div then fulfilled` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `nonex then fulfilled` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `stuck then fulfilled` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
#EVALTRACE EVALTRACE `nested` 0 (LIST EVENT Bob deliver 9)
